From beba9533904ee982edafdf5b92d3c5fc898f55b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChonDoit <thphantomblog@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:24:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/18] treble_app: add the misc hardware, display and
 performance toggles

add device-specific hardware and display toggles to the treble app
for controlling MTK vendor features and display options on GSI.

remove the secure adb toggle since the vndk.rc handler for
persist.sys.phh.adb_secure was replaced by oem_unlock and adbd
hiding triggers in release-builds patch 0003.

add EditTextPreference fields for status bar padding (top, start, end,
bottom) and Quick Settings clock padding (left, right) to the Treble app
UI. These set persist.sys.phh.status_bar_padding_* and
persist.sys.phh.qs_clock_*_padding system properties, allowing users to
fix clipped UI elements on devices with unusual display cutouts.

add three new toggles to the misc settings for SurfaceFlinger control:
latch unsigned buffers, auto latch unsigned (default on) and disable
backpressure propagation. all three require a reboot to take effect.

add a toggle for persist.sys.activity_anim_perf_override which
replaces stock AOSP XML-based activity transition animations with
lightweight programmatic equivalents. fixes lag in Settings and
during app open/close on low-end MTK devices.

replace the prefer hardware codecs toggle with inverted logic
(force software codecs, off by default) setting
persist.sys.phh.force_sw_codecs=true to fix video recording on devices
where the vendor HW encoder rejects PersistentSurface.

add an aggressive memory management switch setting
persist.sys.phh.lmk_tweaks to wire the device_phh_treble lmk_tweaks
prop-handler to a user-facing toggle.

Co-authored-by: Doze-off <viniciussadxxx@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Christopher A. Williamson <contact@chrisaw.io>
